-- title:
--   Valuation rings over A dominating R₀ are Igusa rings
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finset of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace`, i.e. those that are rational, are affine geometric places, and take the value of `jGeomGen` inside `ssJSet q`. Write $\bar F_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, of the field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the divisor expansions of level $M'$, and $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, $H=$ `levelH q M'` being the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; assume $\bar F_{M'}\le F$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\bar F_{M'}$ along $A$ with residue field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ contracting to $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto that function field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$, with every nonzero element scalable into the integers with nonzero residue, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of functions. Assume $R_0$ is pinned to coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\ell\mapsto\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ assign to each point of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ a valuation subring of $F$ such that: $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at $[1:0]$ consists of the $f\in F$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$; and for each $\ell$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ whose reduction modulo $q$ carries $[1:0]$ to $\ell$ and with $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ the preimage of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{[1:0]}$ under the ring homomorphism underlying `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. Then for every valuation subring $\mathcal O$ of $F$ such that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has its image in $\mathcal O$ exactly when it lies in $A$, and such that the image in $F$ of every element of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $\mathcal O$, there exists $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $\mathcal O=\mathcal O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$.
--
--   This is the classification of the prolongations to the full-level field $F$ of the good-reduction (Gauss) valuation of the level-$M'$ field: the only valuation rings of $F$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$ and containing the integers of the constant reduction $R_0$ are the $q+1$ Igusa rings indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$. It feeds the construction of the Igusa charts and of the semistable covering data for $X_H(q^2M')$ over $A$.
